Package: ddmlite
Title: Death Distribution Methods for Death Registration Completeness
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("TODO", "PLACEHOLDER", email = "todo@example.invalid",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = "TODO placeholder: names, e-mail and ORCID are set by the repository owner before any release")
Description: Estimates the completeness of death registration between two censuses with
    death distribution methods (general growth balance, synthetic extinct
    generations and their combination), with or without net migration, by
    area and with paired draws, following the methods described for the
    Global Burden of Disease (GBD) study. Development version: the shared
    infrastructure (draws container, per-cell seeds, age groups, simulated
    country with planted truth) is implemented; most estimation functions
    are documented skeletons. This package is an independent implementation.
    It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by the Institute
    for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME), and it does not contain IHME
    code or data. It is not a successor of the 'DDM' or 'DDMethods'
    packages.
